Build a YouTube-style video platform called **HackTube** that showcases videos the Hacker News community has repeatedly recommended and submitted over the years.

## Core Data
Create a curated dataset of ~47 videos (hand-select well-known tech talks, lectures, and documentaries that are frequently re-posted on HN). For each video, store:
- YouTube ID, title, creator/speaker, year published, duration
- A category (Programming, AI & ML, Computer History, Hardware, Science & Math, Talks & Ideas, Tech & Society, Documentaries, Culture & Fun)
- Estimated HN mention count (how many times submitted/recommended)
- Short description
- "Why it's HN canon" — explanation of why this video resurfaces repeatedly on HN

## Home Page & Browsing
- Fixed header with logo, search bar, and "curated from Y" (HN badge)
- Left sidebar with categories (each with emoji icon) and video counts
- Hero section explaining the concept: "Videos Hacker News can't stop recommending"
- Sticky category chips below hero
- Sort options: Most HN mentions, Newest, Oldest, A→Z
- Responsive grid of video cards (each showing thumbnail, duration, HN mention count as a pill, title, creator, year, category)
- Search across titles, creators, descriptions
- On mobile: hide sidebar, full-width layout

## Watch Page
- Embedded YouTube iframe (youtube-nocookie domain)
- Video title, creator avatar, year, duration, category tag
- HN mention score badge
- Description and "Why it's HN canon" section
- **Live HN discussions**: Fetch real discussion threads from the Algolia HN Search API (search by video title and YouTube ID), show top 8 threads ranked by points with comment count, date, and link to HN
- "Back to browsing" button
- Related videos sidebar (10 videos, sorted by same category then by HN mentions)

## Styling & UX
- Dark theme (inspired by YouTube): dark grays/blacks with orange accent (#ff6600)
- Smooth hover effects on cards
- Hash-based routing (#/watch/[videoId])
- Color-coded creator avatars (deterministic color from name)
- Lazy loading for images with fallback thumbnail sizes
- Responsive design (grid adjusts, nav hides on narrow screens)
- Search input auto-applies when cleared

## Key Behaviors
- All filtering/sorting/search happens client-side on the dataset
- Live thread data is fetched on-demand and cached per video
- If thread fetch fails, show a fallback with link to search HN directly
- Clicking logo or "back" scrolls to top and navigates home

Use vanilla HTML/CSS/JavaScript (no frameworks). Aim for simplicity and clarity over cleverness.
